=== layout: subsection

# Today

## In Person

=== layout: one-panel

# Build From Your Proposal

@body

Open your proposal and find the [*practice task*]{color=#007A00} you described.

- [*Start the instructions*]{color=#007A00} in the Google Doc.
- [*Set up the data*]{color=#007A00} in the Google Sheet and link it from the Doc.
- [*Before you leave*]{color=#007A00}, decide who will finish the instructions, check the expected result, and submit both links.

Start from your proposal today. [*Before Dec 2*]{color=#D40000}, test that someone can follow your Google Doc instructions and complete the activity in your Google Sheet without your help.

@speaker-notes

Ask each group to show what they have and identify what they'll finish next.

- Predictive values: calculate PPV and NPV from simulated test results and check
  the calculations against a worked solution.
- Fertilizer graphs: compare the same plant growth data on two y-axis scales,
  explain which exaggerates the difference, and suggest a correction.
- Focus and sleep graphs: rebuild a misleading chart from the raw data and
  interpret the tradeoff between focus and sleep.
- Reaction time: calculate Cohen's d for regular gamers and non-gamers and
  interpret the size of the difference.

=== layout: subsection

# December 2

## Asynchronous

=== layout: one-panel

# Check That Your Activity Works

@body

- Have [*one group member*]{color=#007A00} follow the Doc instructions from start to finish using a fresh copy of the Sheet. Check that they get the expected result.
- Have [*someone outside your group*]{color=#007A00} verify that they can open both files and make a copy of the Sheet.

[*One activity needs to work by Dec 2.*]{color=#D40000} The rest of the tutorial can still be in progress.

@speaker-notes

For example, show the same fertilizer data in two graphs with different axis scales.
Ask which graph makes the difference look bigger and why. Give a short answer that
explains how the scale changes the impression. A classmate should be able to do the
task and check their own answer.

After Dec 2, check both links from each group. Verify that the data can be copied
and the activity can be completed. Flag any problems before the peer trial.

=== layout: one-panel

# Submit Both Links

@body

- [*Due Wed, Dec 2, 2026, at 11:59 p.m.*]{color=#D40000}
- Have [*one person from each group*]{color=#007A00} submit both links for one working activity.
  - [*Google Doc*]{color=#003FFF} with instructions and a checked answer or interpretation
  - [*Google Sheet*]{color=#003FFF} with data classmates can copy and work with

[https://forms.gle/e2xVpfunpnx7xHrU9](https://forms.gle/e2xVpfunpnx7xHrU9)

